@@ -3,3 +3,32 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`src/index.ts` exports `createRentalService()`, an in-memory service for renting boards and sails.
+It is used from TypeScript or JavaScript as follows:
+
+```ts
+const rentals = createRentalService();
+rentals.addEquipment({ id: 'board-1', kind: 'board', dailyPrice: 2500 }); // 25.00 EUR per day
+rentals.quote({ itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-03T00:00:00Z' });
+// { itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-03T00:00:00Z', total: 5000 }
+rentals.book({ itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-03T00:00:00Z' });
+// { id: 'booking-1', itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-03T00:00:00Z', total: 5000 }
+```
+
+- `addEquipment` takes `{ id, kind, dailyPrice }`, where `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'` and `dailyPrice`
+  is a positive integer number of euro cents per day.
+- `quote` prices a rental without reserving the item. `book` reserves it and returns a booking with an `id`.
+- Periods start and end at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day after the last day. A
+  period that ends where another begins does not overlap it. Each booking is priced as whole days times
+  the daily price.
+- `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period that is not allowed. `book` also throws when
+  the item is already booked for any part of the period.
+- Booking ids are sequential within a service (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...), so the same calls always
+  give the same ids.
+- Cancellation is not implemented yet.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`. The tests run on the TypeScript source directly with Node's built-in
+type stripping (Node 22.18 or later), so no build step or dependency is needed.
